Package: dualctl
Type: Package
Title: Dual Control and Active Learning for Model-Based Sequential Optimization
Version: 0.1.0
Date: 2026-10-27
Authors@R: person("Hans", "Schepers", email = "hans.schepers@gmail.com",
                  role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: A model-agnostic toolbox for sequential optimisation of a physical
    process when the model structure is roughly trusted, parameters are
    uncertain and observations are sparse and noisy (model-rich, data-poor).
    One season or campaign is one trajectory to learn from and act on. The
    engine combines a hierarchical parameter estimator (extended or ensemble
    Kalman filter on a parameter-augmented state), an identifiability module
    (sensitivities, Fisher information, Cramer-Rao bounds), receding-horizon
    control with discrete events, probing strategies (dither, information-aware
    MPC, Thompson sampling, EVSI targeting), an advisor that ranks control
    changes, Shapley attribution of savings, and an experiment layer with
    production and probe arms. Models are plug-in files plus a YAML config. A
    heat-exchanger fouling demo and a toy decay model are included.
